 ## Background
-The method is based on the "Fast Voxel Traversal" algorithm, implemented in Rust in the repository `AThilenius/fast-voxel-traversal-rs` [S1, unofficial]. It extends the classic 3D DDA ray traversal algorithm by adding an initial AABB intersection test to handle rays that do not intersect the volume bounds, allowing for early termination. This approach is particularly useful in volume rendering pipelines where rays are cast from every pixel, and many may miss the volume entirely.
+The method implements a voxel traversal algorithm using an AABB test, calculates steps, deltas, and t_max values, and iterates through voxels [S1, unofficial].
 
